<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">People's State of Hesse</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1945 CE · capital Darmstadt</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Republican successor of the Grand Duchy of Hesse, a Social Democratic state on both sides of the Rhine.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ernest-louis-grand-duke-of-hesse">Grand Duke Ernest Louis</a> was deposed in November 1918, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-hesse">Hesse-Darmstadt</a> became the People's State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>, with a democratic constitution adopted in December 1919. It kept the grand duchy's three provinces: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/starkenburg">Starkenburg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-hesse">Upper Hesse</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giessen">Giessen</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhenish-hesse">Rhenish Hesse</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-worms">Worms</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Social Democrats led the state for most of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar">Weimar</a> years under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carl-ulrich">Carl Ulrich</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhenish-hesse">Rhenish Hesse</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a> were under French occupation until 1930. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a> had a technical university and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merck-group">Merck</a> chemical company. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nazism">Nazis</a> took power in March 1933 under Reich governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jakob-sprenger">Jakob Sprenger</a>, and the Jewish communities of Mainz and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-worms">Worms</a>, among the oldest in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, were destroyed.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1945 the parts east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> were combined with Prussian territories into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greater-hesse">Greater Hesse</a> in the American zone, now the state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhenish-hesse">Rhenish Hesse</a> went to the French zone and later to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland-palatinate">Rhineland-Palatinate</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/peoples-state-of-hesse.jpg" alt="People's State of Hesse" width="320" height="256"><figcaption>Image: David Liuzzo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flagge_Gro%C3%9Fherzogtum_Hessen_ohne_Wappen.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1945 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Darmstadt</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Carl Ulrich, Jakob Sprenger</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism, Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Volksstaat Hessen</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1932&amp;focus=peoples-state-of-hesse" aria-label="People's State of Hesse on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4878 442 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where People's State of Hesse lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5198 698L5198 698M5198 698L5300 622M5198 698L5300 622"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5198 698h0M5300 622h0M5300 622h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5198 698h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5198 698h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1932&amp;focus=peoples-state-of-hesse">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
